      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3d051d22-b5b2-5397-997c-ac094ee87666",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: The Apple Dumpling Gang, Something Wicked This Way Comes, The Apple Dumpling Gang Rides Again, The Shaggy D.A., The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh, The Fox and the Hound, The Outlaw Josey Wales\n- People: Bill Bixby, Jack Clayton, Ray Bradbury, Buddy Baker, Paul J. Smith, Bruce M. Fischer, Clint Eastwood\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions\n- Roles: Russell Donovan, Mr. Coogar\n- Topics: California Gold Rush\n\nFacts:\n- In 1975, Walt Disney Productions produced The Apple Dumpling Gang, an American comedy-western film.\n- In 1975, The Apple Dumpling Gang starred Bill Bixby as Russell Donovan, a slick gambler who is duped into caring for a group of orphans who eventually strike gold during the California Gold Rush.\n- In 1975, Buddy Baker helped score the Disney film The Apple Dumpling Gang with Paul J. Smith.\n- In 1976, Bruce M. Fischer played a rapist in Clint Eastwood's film The Outlaw Josey Wales.\n- In 1976, Buddy Baker helped score the Disney film The Shaggy D.A. with Paul J. Smith.\n- In 1977, Buddy Baker helped score the Disney film The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh with Paul J. Smith.\n- In 1979, Buddy Baker helped score the Disney film The Apple Dumpling Gang Rides Again with Paul J. Smith.\n- In 1981, Buddy Baker helped score the Disney film The Fox and the Hound with Paul J. Smith.\n- In 1983, Walt Disney Productions produced Something Wicked This Way Comes, an American horror fantasy film directed by Jack Clayton.\n- In 1983, Ray Bradbury wrote the screenplay for Something Wicked This Way Comes, based on his novel of the same name.\n- In 1983, Bruce M. Fischer played Mr. Coogar in Something Wicked This Way Comes.\n- Buddy Baker was an American composer born on January 4, 1918, and he died on July 26, 2002.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f1b5c72f-6d76-5241-b012-882f8b342d10",
        "text": "Page: The Apple Dumpling Gang (film). Sentence: The Apple Dumpling Gang is a 1975 American comedy-western film produced by Walt Disney Productions about a slick gambler named Russell Donovan (Bill Bixby) who is duped into taking care of a group of orphans who eventually strike gold during the California Gold Rush.\nPage: Something Wicked This Way Comes (film). Sentence: Something Wicked This Way Comes is a 1983 American horror fantasy film directed by Jack Clayton and produced by Walt Disney Productions from a screenplay written by Ray Bradbury, based on his novel of the same name.\nPage: Buddy Baker (composer). Sentence: Norman Dale \"Buddy\" Baker (January 4, 1918 – July 26, 2002) was an American composer who, together with Paul J. Smith, scored many Disney films, such as \"The Apple Dumpling Gang\" in 1975, \"The Apple Dumpling Gang Rides Again\" in 1979, \"The Shaggy D.A.\" in 1976, \"The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh\" in 1977, and \"The Fox and the Hound\" in 1981.\nPage: Bruce M. Fischer. Sentence: Fischer also played a rapist in Clint Eastwood's \"The Outlaw Josey Wales\" (1976), and Mr. Coogar in the film \"Something Wicked This Way Comes\" (1983).",
